From 541b6d4b4352eb33b587c52258ca11bae9ed0903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: map a picture of HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision
 by its own tone curve in Low-Latency

In Dolby Vision Low-Latency the player maps the picture to the display, and a
picture of HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision was mapped from the level 1 that its
metadata are made of: the BT.2390 curve from the brightest of its HDR10+
statistics. The tone curve that the studio made for the scene (SMPTE ST
2094-40 8.7, the knee point and the Bezier curve for a display of a given
peak) was left out, although nothing in Low-Latency leaves it no place: the
display shows the picture as it comes.

dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus() gives the renderer the HDR10+ metadata of the
picture that it draws, as dvbridge_hdr10plus_plain() takes them. In
Low-Latency, a picture whose metadata carry a curve that can be used is mapped
by it as an HDR10+ picture adapted to the display is, by the same function and
table (map_hdr10plus(): libplacebo's pl_tone_map_st2094_40 from the scene's
brightest, a table of 1024 entries made again where the metadata change), to
the target of the Low-Latency mapping; the gamut mapping, the black of the
display and the peak held are as before. Everything else draws the same bytes
as before: no metadata, metadata without a curve (level 1 guides the curve of
the mapping), HLG sent as Dolby Vision, the test pattern, Dolby Vision
Standard (the display maps the picture there, and nothing of this is read) and
Dolby Vision of a video's own.

Fail closed: metadata that do not hold (a value not finite or out of its
range) count as none; a render with the curve that fails, where the picture
draws without it, is made again without it, and the rest of the stream is
mapped without it (dvbridge_render_take_notes(): hdr10plus_ll_failed), so no
picture is lost and no frame is drawn twice after that; a reset tries it
again. The reference of the check of the bytes takes main's metadata.
dvbridge_render_hdr10plus_curve() says whether the last picture was mapped by
the curve.

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (llvmpipe and zink), a 3840x2160 neutral
ramp of every 10-bit code, its metadata made as the decoder makes them, the
transport of 12 bits decoded as a receiver reads it, against an independent
computation of ST 2094-40 8.7.4 on the picture that the metadata of profile
8.1 describe: the curve of Tears of Steel (a display of 400 cd/m2) and 13
synthetic curves, on a display of the curve's target and of other peaks (600
to 1387 cd/m2, and the scene's brightest), 31 cases on each: at most 0.59 to
0.64 of a code of 12-bit PQ (the 12-bit transport alone rounds by up to 0.58),
0.27 to 0.37 on average; the ramp neutral and never going down. (The HDR10
codes themselves are up to 0.87 of a code above that picture at the top, by
the precision of the YCbCr to RGB matrix of profile 8.1, 9574/8192, which
every picture sent so has, before this change as after it.) On a display of
the curve's target, the mapping from level 1 was up to 184 codes and 71 on
average from the curve; on one of 1387 cd/m2, the curve moves the picture from
it by 48 codes on average.

The same bytes as before, frame by frame: real Dolby Vision (profile 7 FEL, 64
frames) in Low-Latency, in the IPT and BT.2020 transports and shown as HDR10;
HLG and HDR10 sent as Dolby Vision in Low-Latency; in Low-Latency, no HDR10+
metadata given, metadata without a curve, and pictures without metadata among
pictures with a curve; Dolby Vision Standard and the test pattern with the
metadata given; a display of its own gamut and black; HDR10 and HDR10+ adapted
to the display and mapped to SDR.

A frame costs the same as before within the noise of the software renderer
(3840x2160 on llvmpipe: 182 to 189 ms with the curve, 177 to 187 ms without; a
new scene every frame, 183 to 184 against 177 to 186). The table of the curve
is made only where the metadata change, on the thread that draws and with no
wait for the GPU: 0.14 to 0.19 ms of one core, against 2.6 to 5.2 us for the
BT.2390 one.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h |  26 +++++++
 2 files changed, 146 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
index 7bf806c..63aec86 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ enum {
     NOTE_TRIM_FAILED = 8192,
     NOTE_HDR10PLUS_CURVE = 16384,
     NOTE_HDR10PLUS_STATISTICS = 32768,
+    NOTE_HDR10PLUS_LL_FAILED = 65536,
 };
 
 /* Hades: the bridge's own passes that are timed (dvbridge_render_time_passes()), each with a few
@@ -192,6 +193,14 @@ struct dvbridge_renderer {
      * ll_mapping, packed without metadata; ll_pattern, the test pattern in its place */
     bool low_latency, ll_pattern;
     struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping ll_mapping;
+    /* Hades: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision in Low-Latency (dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus()): the HDR10+ metadata of
+     * the pictures drawn now (present false: none); the render in hand maps its picture by their tone curve
+     * (ll_curve_tried), the last render drew its picture so (ll_curve_drawn), and a render with it failed on this
+     * GPU, so the pictures of the rest of the stream are mapped without it (ll_curve_failed; ll_curve_retry()) */
+    struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus ll_hdr10plus;
+    bool ll_curve_tried, ll_curve_drawn, ll_curve_failed;
+    /* ... and the last render drew a picture without the curve it has, because of ll_curve_failed */
+    bool ll_curve_held;
     /* Hades: the trim pass (dvbridge_trims.h): the render in hand has one (trim_tried); one could
        not be drawn on
      * this GPU, and pictures are mapped without it from here on (trim_failed; trim_retry()) */
@@ -638,7 +647,10 @@ static void map_to_display(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hd
                            const struct dvbridge_level1 *level1);
 static void map_hdr10plus(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *m,
                           struct pl_color_space *source, struct pl_color_map_params *params,
-                          const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h);
+                          const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h, bool low_latency);
+static bool ll_curve_usable(struct dvbridge_renderer *r);
+static bool ll_curve_retry(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool ok);
+static void ll_curve_kept(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool ok);
 static const struct dvbridge_level1 *level1_noted(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const void *metadata,
                                                   size_t bytes, struct dvbridge_level1 *level1);
 static bool trim_prepare(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *m,
@@ -734,6 +746,9 @@ void dvbridge_renderer_reset(struct dvbridge_renderer *r)
     dvbridge_reset(r->context);
     r->noted = r->fresh = 0;
     r->trim_failed = false;
+    /* Hades: (a new stream: no HDR10+ metadata until they are given, and the curve is tried again) */
+    r->ll_hdr10plus = (struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus){0};
+    r->ll_curve_failed = false;
 }
 
 void dvbridge_render_set_frame_period(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, double period)
@@ -775,6 +790,7 @@ bool dvbridge_render_take_notes(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, struct dvbridge_ren
     notes->trim_failed = r->fresh & NOTE_TRIM_FAILED;
     notes->hdr10plus_curve = r->fresh & NOTE_HDR10PLUS_CURVE;
     notes->hdr10plus_statistics = r->fresh & NOTE_HDR10PLUS_STATISTICS;
+    notes->hdr10plus_ll_failed = r->fresh & NOTE_HDR10PLUS_LL_FAILED;
     r->fresh = 0;
     return true;
 }
@@ -1446,6 +1462,7 @@ static bool render(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *source,
     r->residual_drawn = false;
     r->packed = packed != NULL;
     r->gui_drawn = 0;
+    r->ll_curve_drawn = r->ll_curve_held = false; /* (Hades: dvbridge_render_hdr10plus_curve()) */
     dvbridge_candidate_destroy(r->pending);
     r->pending = NULL;
     /* Hades: the picture that a composed render of the source transport made in the tiles of what
@@ -1594,6 +1611,14 @@ static bool render(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *source,
                        r->base_transfer == DVBRIDGE_BASE_HLG_TO_PQ
                            ? NULL
                            : level1_noted(r, metadata, bytes, &level1));
+        /* Hades: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision: a picture whose HDR10+ metadata carry a tone curve that can be used
+         * is mapped by it, as an HDR10+ picture adapted to the display is (dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus()); its
+         * level 1, made from the same metadata, is then not what the curve maps from. Anything else as before. */
+        const bool curve = ll_curve_usable(r);
+        r->ll_curve_tried = curve && !r->ll_curve_failed;
+        r->ll_curve_held = curve && r->ll_curve_failed;
+        if (r->ll_curve_tried)
+            map_hdr10plus(r, &r->ll_mapping, &image.color, &ll_color, &r->ll_hdr10plus, true);
         params.color_map_params = &ll_color;
         mask.low_latency = true;
         mask.peak = pl_hdr_rescale(PL_HDR_NITS, PL_HDR_PQ, r->ll_mapping.peak);
@@ -1672,6 +1697,7 @@ static bool render(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *source,
     else if (!clean)
         r->not_drawn = WHY_PLACEBO_ERRORS;
     r->ready = r->ready && clean;
+    r->ll_curve_drawn = r->ready && mask.low_latency && r->ll_curve_tried;
     /* (Hades: a picture over HLG whose RPU declares PQ may be drawn by libplacebo's reshaping.) What
      * the render composed, and why a base layer that is not in PQ was not composed, are of the render
      * as its errors leave it, as render_hdr10() has them: a render that they fail composed nothing. */
@@ -1732,8 +1758,10 @@ bool dvbridge_render_rgb(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *sou
     struct dvbridge_gl_state state;
     save_gl_state(&state);
     const bool fine = r && fine_gamut_table(r, true);
-    if (r)
+    if (r) {
         r->trim_tried = false;
+        r->ll_curve_tried = false;
+    }
     bool ok = render_bars_first(r, source, metadata, bytes, pts, el_pts, geometry, NULL, false);
     /* Hades: with the standard gamut table where the finer one could not be made */
     if (r && gamut_table_retry(r, fine, ok)) {
@@ -1745,6 +1773,15 @@ bool dvbridge_render_rgb(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *sou
         ok = render_bars_first(r, source, metadata, bytes, pts, el_pts, geometry, NULL, false);
         trim_kept(r, ok);
     }
+    /* Hades: without the HDR10+ tone curve where it could not be drawn (Low-Latency) */
+    if (r && ll_curve_retry(r, ok)) {
+        ok = render_bars_first(r, source, metadata, bytes, pts, el_pts, geometry, NULL, false);
+        ll_curve_kept(r, ok);
+    }
+    /* (a picture drawn without the curve it has, because this GPU does not draw it: noted once in a stream, also
+     * where that was found while the ways of drawing were made ready, whose notes are not kept) */
+    if (r && ok && r->ll_curve_held)
+        note(r, NOTE_HDR10PLUS_LL_FAILED);
     restore_gl_state(&state);
     /* Hades: what was to be drawn over this frame (dvbridge_render_set_drawn()) is this frame's */
     if (r) {
@@ -2268,10 +2305,12 @@ bool dvbridge_render_gamut_made(const struct dvbridge_renderer *r, struct dvbrid
  * that brightest. Nothing changes for a picture without them: the same parameters as before, bit for bit. The
  * table of the curve (in PQ, libplacebo's: 1024 entries for the picture's own curve, below, else 256) is made
  * again only where the metadata change, once a scene, not for each frame (pl_tone_map_params_equal()); the gamut
- * table does not depend on them. */
+ * table does not depend on them. Hades: the same for a picture of Dolby Vision Low-Latency made from its HDR10+
+ * metadata (low_latency: the notes say so), where the caller asks for it (one with a tone curve that can be used:
+ * ll_curve_usable()); the source is then the picture that its identity mapping reconstructs, BT.2020 PQ. */
 static void map_hdr10plus(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *m,
                           struct pl_color_space *source, struct pl_color_map_params *params,
-                          const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h)
+                          const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h, bool low_latency)
 {
     if (!h || !h->present)
         return;
@@ -2311,7 +2350,79 @@ static void map_hdr10plus(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_hdr
         r->notes.hdr10plus.curve = curve;
         r->notes.hdr10plus_peak = m->peak;
         r->notes.hdr10plus_sdr = m->target == DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TARGET_SDR;
+        r->notes.hdr10plus_ll = low_latency;
+    }
+}
+
+/* Hades: a range of a value of the HDR10+ metadata that the mapping takes */
+static bool value_within(float v, float lo, float hi)
+{
+    return isfinite(v) && v >= lo && v <= hi;
+}
+
+void dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h)
+{
+    if (!r)
+        return;
+    r->ll_hdr10plus = (struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus){0};
+    if (!h || !h->present)
+        return;
+    /* what dvbridge_hdr10plus_plain() gives: the statistics in cd/m2, of a brightest above 0 and an average above
+     * 0; a curve for a display of 1 to 10000 cd/m2, its knee point and anchors in [0, 1] (fail closed: anything
+     * else counts as no metadata) */
+    bool holds = value_within(h->scene_avg, 0.0f, 10000.0f) && h->scene_avg > 0.0f;
+    float brightest = 0.0f;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
+        holds = holds && value_within(h->scene_max[i], 0.0f, 10000.0f);
+        brightest = holds && h->scene_max[i] > brightest ? h->scene_max[i] : brightest;
+    }
+    holds = holds && brightest > 0.0f;
+    if (holds && h->curve) {
+        holds = value_within(h->target, 1.0f, 10000.0f) && value_within(h->knee_x, 0.0f, 1.0f) &&
+                value_within(h->knee_y, 0.0f, 1.0f) && h->anchors >= 1 && h->anchors <= DVBRIDGE_HDR10PLUS_ANCHORS_MAX;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; holds && i < h->anchors; ++i)
+            holds = value_within(h->anchor[i], 0.0f, 1.0f);
     }
+    if (holds)
+        r->ll_hdr10plus = *h;
+}
+
+bool dvbridge_render_hdr10plus_curve(const struct dvbridge_renderer *r)
+{
+    return r && r->ll_curve_drawn;
+}
+
+/* Hades: the picture of the render in hand (Low-Latency) is to be mapped by the tone curve of its HDR10+ metadata
+ * (dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus()): there is one that can be used, of a picture in PQ (not HLG sent as Dolby
+ * Vision). The test pattern takes the place of the picture: nothing to map. Where this GPU was found not to draw
+ * it (ll_curve_failed), the picture is mapped without it (render()). */
+static bool ll_curve_usable(struct dvbridge_renderer *r)
+{
+    const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *h = &r->ll_hdr10plus;
+    return r->low_latency && !r->ll_pattern && r->base_transfer == DVBRIDGE_BASE_PQ && h->present && h->curve &&
+           h->anchors >= 1 && h->anchors <= DVBRIDGE_HDR10PLUS_ANCHORS_MAX;
+}
+
+/* Hades: after a render with the HDR10+ tone curve (Low-Latency) that failed: whether to make it again without it
+ * (the curve is noted as failed, and the errors that libplacebo keeps reset). The caller makes it again; where that
+ * draws, the curve was why, and the pictures of the rest of the stream are mapped without it (the note is made by
+ * the render that draws a picture without the curve it has: dvbridge_render_rgb()); where it fails as well, it was
+ * not, and the curve is tried again with the next picture (ll_curve_kept()). */
+static bool ll_curve_retry(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool ok)
+{
+    if (ok || !r->ll_curve_tried)
+        return false;
+    r->ll_curve_failed = true;
+    r->ll_curve_tried = false;
+    pl_renderer_reset_errors(r->renderer, NULL);
+    dvbridge_gl_drain_errors();
+    return true;
+}
+
+static void ll_curve_kept(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, bool ok)
+{
+    if (!ok)
+        r->ll_curve_failed = false;
 }
 
 /* Hades: the trim pass of the metadata of a picture mapped to a display
@@ -2670,7 +2781,7 @@ static bool render_hdr10(struct dvbridge_renderer *r, const struct pl_frame *sou
                        level1_noted(r, metadata, bytes, &level1));
         /* Hades: a plain PQ picture with HDR10+ metadata: guided by them (dvbridge_hdr10plus_map.h) */
         if (plain && !plain->hlg)
-            map_hdr10plus(r, &r->hdr10_mapping, &image.color, &mapping, &plain->hdr10plus);
+            map_hdr10plus(r, &r->hdr10_mapping, &image.color, &mapping, &plain->hdr10plus, false);
         params.color_map_params = &mapping;
         if (!plain)
             trim_prepare(r, &r->hdr10_mapping, metadata, bytes, &trim);
@@ -3042,6 +3153,10 @@ bool dvbridge_render_reference(struct dvbridge_renderer *ref, const struct dvbri
     ref->low_latency = main->low_latency;
     ref->ll_pattern = main->ll_pattern;
     ref->ll_mapping = main->ll_mapping;
+    /* (Hades: and the HDR10+ tone curve of its picture, where it maps the picture by it, unless main found that
+     * this GPU does not draw it) */
+    ref->ll_hdr10plus = main->ll_hdr10plus;
+    ref->ll_curve_failed = main->ll_curve_failed;
     /* (and the gamut table of its mapping, which changes the picture on purpose) */
     ref->gamut_asked = main->gamut_asked;
     ref->gamut_fine_failed = main->gamut_fine_failed;
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
index 5063429..d54f71c 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_render.h
@@ -99,6 +99,11 @@ struct dvbridge_render_notes {
     struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus hdr10plus;
     float hdr10plus_peak;
     bool hdr10plus_sdr;
+    /* Hades: ... hdr10plus_ll, that picture was one of Dolby Vision Low-Latency, made from its HDR10+ metadata
+     * (dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus()), mapped by its tone curve; hdr10plus_ll_failed, a render with that curve
+     * could not be drawn on this GPU, and the pictures of the rest of the stream are mapped from their level 1, as
+     * without it (none was lost) */
+    bool hdr10plus_ll, hdr10plus_ll_failed;
 };
 /* false when there is nothing new since the last call */
 bool dvbridge_render_take_notes(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, struct dvbridge_render_notes *notes);
@@ -261,6 +266,27 @@ bool dvbridge_render_gamut_made(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer,
 bool dvbridge_render_set_low_latency(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer,
                                      const struct dvbridge_hdr10_mapping *mapping);
 bool dvbridge_render_low_latency(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer);
+/* Hades: HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision, in Low-Latency: the HDR10+ metadata (SMPTE ST 2094-40) of the picture that
+ * the renders from now on draw, as dvbridge_hdr10plus_plain() takes them, for a picture whose Dolby Vision metadata
+ * are made from them (dvbridge_hdr10plus.h: an identity mapping and level 1 from their statistics). In Low-Latency
+ * the player maps the picture to the display: a picture whose metadata carry a tone curve that can be used is
+ * mapped by that curve as dvbridge_render_plain() maps an HDR10+ picture (map_hdr10plus(): libplacebo's
+ * pl_tone_map_st2094_40 on the Bezier curve, from the brightest of the scene, a table of 1024 entries made again
+ * where the metadata change), to the target of the Low-Latency mapping; the rest of the render is as before (the
+ * gamut mapping, the black of the display, the peak held, the transport). Everything else is drawn as before, bit
+ * for bit: none given (NULL, the default), metadata without such a curve (level 1 guides the curve of the mapping,
+ * as always), HLG sent as Dolby Vision, the test pattern, and Low-Latency off (with Dolby Vision Standard the
+ * display maps the picture, and nothing of this is read). Metadata that do not hold (a value that is not finite or
+ * out of its range) count as none. Fail closed: a render with the curve that fails, where the same picture draws
+ * without it, is made again without it, and the pictures of the rest of the stream are drawn without it (the note
+ * hdr10plus_ll_failed); no picture is lost to it. The caller sets it for every picture, with that picture's own
+ * metadata (and what a picture without metadata of its own gets): it is kept until it is set again, and a reset
+ * takes it back to none. The reference renderer of a check of the bytes takes main's (it changes the picture on
+ * purpose). dvbridge_render_hdr10plus_curve(): the last render mapped its picture by the curve. */
+#define DVBRIDGE_RENDER_HDR10PLUS_LL 1
+void dvbridge_render_set_hdr10plus(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer,
+                                   const struct dvbridge_plain_hdr10plus *hdr10plus);
+bool dvbridge_render_hdr10plus_curve(const struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer);
 /* Hades: HDR over the tunnel (DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB): an HDR10, HLG or HDR10+ picture (or a
    Dolby Vision
  * one reconstructed as HDR10) that is sent as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits packed in the RGB 8 bpc
-- 
2.53.0

